{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"a\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"arr\" expr=\"[1,2]\"/></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <onentry><foreach array=\"arr\" item=\"1bad\" index=\"i\"><log expr=\"i\"/></foreach></onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-foreach-item-digit.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-foreach-item-digit.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":4,"byteOffset":209,"endColumn":45,"endLine":4,"startColumn":41,"startLine":4},"insertedContent":{"text":"item1bad"}}]}],"description":{"text":"prefix the name with `item`: `item1bad`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-foreach-item-digit.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":4,"startColumn":41,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<foreach item>` must be a variable name, but `1bad` starts with a digit\n\n**Note:** `<foreach>` assigns each array element (`item`) and its position (`index`) to a variable with this name, creating it when it is not declared; the name must be a legal identifier of the `ecmascript` data model\n\n**Help:** use a name that starts with a letter or `$` and contains only ASCII letters, digits, `_`, and `$` (the ECMAScript data model reserves names that start with `_` for system variables)\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.6 <foreach>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`<foreach item>` must be a variable name, but `1bad` starts with a digit"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":213,"start":209},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML039"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`location`, `idlocation`, `namelist` items, and `<foreach item/index>` must name an assignable place; SCXML 1.0 defines the run-time outcome of one that does not, so the document compiles: §5.9.2 \"If a location expression cannot be evaluated to yield a valid location, the SCXML processor MUST place the error 'error.execution' in the internal event queue\", and §4.6 \"if 'item' does not specify a legal variable name, the SCXML processor MUST terminate execution of the <foreach> element and the block that contains it, and place the error error.execution on the internal event queue\". In ECMAScript an assignable place is a variable or a property access such as `data.field` or `data[0]`; in XPath it is an expression that selects existing nodes, such as `$data` or `$data/field` (`a.b` is one variable name containing a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: ECMAScript: use a variable name or a member expression such as `data.field`; XPath: use a `$`-rooted path to a declared variable such as `$data/field`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML039` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LocationExpressions","id":"SCXML039","name":"SCXML039","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a location is not assignable in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}